during your visit michel bachelet the  high commissioner for human rights met  with the bangladesh prime minister  sheikh hasina and government high  officials as well as civil society and  rights groups  the high commissioner made clear that  extrajudicial killings and forced  disappearances were huge obstacles in  the pursuit of justice  i raised my deep concern about this  serious allegation with government  ministers and highlighted the need for  an impartial independent and transparent  investigation into these allegations  accompanied by security sector reform  several international and local human  rights organizations have urged the u.n  high commissioner for human rights to  press the bangladesh government to  ensure full accountability for the human  rights abuses that still persist in the  country  bashley also raised her concern about  self-censorship in bangladesh media a  consequence of the digital security act  we have submitted our recommendations  for repeal and revision of certain  provisions of the act  with a view to ensuring their compliance  with international human rights law and  standards and preventing arbitrary  application or misuse  bashley also visited the world's largest  refugee camp in cox's bazar on the  southeast coast  the international community must sustain  its efforts to bangladesh in its  response and press myanmar to create  conditions for return address the root  causes and pursue accountability  she met with several refugees in the  camp  i told her we do want to return to  myanmar but we don't want to face  repression and persecution again and  that needs to be ensured  she assured us that our demands will be  presented accordingly  not only i'm visiting here michelle  bachelor said the importance of  bangladesh's humanitarian contribution  and its historical significance cannot  be overstated  unfortunately the current situation  across the border means that the  conditions are not right for returns  representation must always be conducted  in a voluntary and dignified manner only  when safe and sustainable conditions  exist in myanmar finally she asked her  bangladeshi host to include members of  the rohingya community in the country's  social and economic sectors while they  were in exile tanvid choudhary  al-jazeera dhaka
 

